SUMMARY:Dinner: Mild Chickpea & Potato Curry with Yogurt Raita
DESCRIPTION:A mild chickpea and potato curry served with yogurt raita.\n\nS
 erves 2\n\nIngredients:\n- 1 can (15 oz) chickpeas\, drained and rinsed\n-
  2 medium potatoes\, peeled and diced\n- 1 can (14 oz) diced tomatoes\n- 1
  small onion\, diced\n- 2 cloves garlic\, minced\n- 1 tbsp fresh ginger\, 
 minced\n- 1 tbsp mild curry powder\n- 1/2 tsp turmeric\n- 1 cup vegetable 
 broth\n- 2 tbsp olive oil\n- Salt\, to taste\n- 1/2 cup plain yogurt\n- 1/
 2 cucumber\, chopped\, plus a pinch of cumin (for the raita)\n\nInstructio
 ns:\n1. Heat olive oil in a large pot over medium heat. Saute onion until 
 soft\, about 5 minutes.\n2. Add garlic and ginger\, cook 1 minute.\n3. Sti
 r in curry powder and turmeric\, toast 30 seconds.\n4. Add potatoes\, chic
 kpeas\, diced tomatoes\, and vegetable broth. Simmer 20-25 minutes until p
 otatoes are tender.\n5. Season with salt to taste -- keep it mild\, no add
 ed chili.\n6. For the raita\, stir chopped cucumber and a pinch of cumin i
 nto the plain yogurt.\n7. Serve the curry with rice and the raita on the s
 ide.\n8. Kevin: add cooked chicken thighs for extra protein.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
